                'en' => 'After the accident, SNCF limited trains to 40 km/h on the section until the mayor banned vehicles over 3.5 tonnes from the crossing on 14 November 2011 and the prefect diverted them. Safety works were announced for March 2012. According to Wikipedia, the level crossing was eventually closed: a 240 m viaduct, built by the département downstream, opened in December 2019.',
