                'en' => 'On the judicial side, RFF (now SNCF Réseau) and SNCF were placed under formal investigation in 2014. According to the French Wikipedia article, the Rennes criminal court tried the case in April 2018: the lorry driver was sentenced to 36 months suspended prison and a five-year ban on driving heavy goods vehicles, the two companies to fines of 300,000 euros each; the appeal court upheld these convictions on 10 December 2019, and the Court of Cassation reportedly dismissed SNCF\'s appeal on 6 December 2021.',
